index 1d39b57..ea6a1f0 100644
--- a/development/README.md
+++ b/development/README.md
@@ -105,3 +105,50 @@ I2C operation still require device validation.
 The agreed additive TWI/UART stage and subsequent measured legacy-function
 replacement stage are described in [hardware development tracks](../docs/hardware_development_tracks.md).
 Keep binary-different development replacements separate from the exact baseline.
+
+
+## MCU–FPGA SPI and configuration diagnostic
+
+`@FPGA` reads diagnostic registers 40–44. `@FPGATEST` verifies IDs 504D/5350,
+then writes and reads 32 walking-one/zero patterns at register 40, restoring and
+reading back its initial value. It refuses writes if the image IDs do not match.
+The Kintex diagnostic derives its active-low CS protocol from the original
+`SCKI/SPI_CS` slave, not the unrelated `HSCK/HSEL` interface. SPIC uses MSB-first
+mode 0; each operation is a 16-bit header plus 16-bit word. PLL/DAC select lines
+must be inactive. Each transaction restores SPIC control and releases CS.
+
+`@CFG` reports raw PORTD input/output (INIT_B bit 2, DONE bit 3, PROGRAM_B output
+bit 1). `@CFG HOLD` asserts PROGRAM_B, **destroys FPGA SRAM configuration**, and
+makes SPIE own the configuration bus. Once DONE reads low, `@FLASHID` sends 9F;
+`@FLASHREAD 000000 10` sends 03 and reads at most 16 bytes. No WREN, programming
+or erase commands exist. `@CFG BOOT` disables SPIE, releases its GPIO outputs
+and raises PROGRAM_B. Its reply confirms a request, not successful configuration;
+poll INIT/DONE and apply a deadline before reporting success. Flash contents may
+be unknown, so arrange JTAG restoration of the known diagnostic before this test.
+
+The recovered power/FPGA retry state machine remains active, including its
+roughly five-second retry. HOLD is therefore a short inspection operation, not
+a persistent programming mode. Verify ownership on every read; a lost lease
+returns ERR CONFIG OWNERSHIP. Perform these operations under the PM12 board
+lock. Do not run them through the default read-only UART capture script.
+
+Host tests cover read/write framing, both interrupt states, every byte timeout,
+CS/controller restoration, image guard and read-only flash opcodes. GHDL tests
+the slave; Vivado implementation of the combined SPI/Ethernet/I2C diagnostic
+passed. MCU programming, physical SPI, flash ownership and boot completion
+remain NOT_RUN until the identified UART is connected.
+
+
+## Physical checkpoint2026-10-15
+
+Diagnostic code f9869c9 was programmed via Atmel-ICE PDI after a physical full
+backup. Original physical FLASH matched golden exactly. Application-only page
+programming and full readback PASS; boot, EEPROM, fuse/lock, user/production
+signatures were unchanged. Physical fuse4 F3 was retained (historical ELF E3
+was not applied). UART/device reads and672 FPGA SPI walking patterns PASS.
+Config-flash JEDEC016017, read-only ownership/data/release PASS; DONE was not
+observed in a2s boot window, so flash boot remains unconfirmed. PGTIME reports
+NOT_STARTED; physical startup/fault timing remains unvalidated. No MCU INA
+driver exists in this candidate. Input-only I2C FPGA diagnostic504d5a02 remains
+in SRAM; MCU diagnostic remains running. Authoritative raw traces/summary:
+`/home/codex-hil/fit-bringup/evidence/pm12-fw-validation-2026-10-15/`.
